<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="77114" href="schedule/2022/fall/GEOL/593/77114.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2022" href="schedule/2022.xml">2022</calendarYear><term id="120228" href="schedule/2022/fall.xml">Fall 2022</term><subject id="GEOL" href="schedule/2022/fall/GEOL.xml">Geology</subject><course id="593" href="schedule/2022/fall/GEOL/593.xml">Advanced Studies in Geology</course></parents><sectionNumber>L1 </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Magmatism &amp; Plate Tectonics</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>This course will explore there rich variety of Earth’s magmatism occurring at various plate tectonic settings on the planet.  It will cover formation of  magma in the mantle and processes in the crust leading to either eruption as an extrusive rock or emplacement as an intrusive rock.  Connections to climate and ore deposition will also be discussed. The course will consist of readings and discussions.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2022-08-22Z</startDate><endDate>2022-12-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>10:00 AM</start><end>12:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>F      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>2084</roomNumber><buildingName>Natural History Building</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Lundstrom" firstName="C">Lundstrom, C</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>